Importing Data for the Simulation
Import Data for the Simulation
Introduces you on how to work with data provided by the departments of the plant you are modeling, such
as production lists, data, which machines output, etc. while you create your simulation model.
Importing Data for the Simulation
10-1314 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

As a rule you will import this data from a spreadsheet program, such as Microsoft Excel, or from a
database, into a Plant Simulation list or table. From the data bulk you will have to filter out the data you
actually do need to use for your simulation project. The material flow objects can then access these lists
and use the data for the simulation.
Naturally you may also want to export some or all of the data, which the simulation runs created, so that
you can use and manipulate it in other programs.
Importing and Exporting Data
Import and Export Data
Plant Simulation provides a number of ways to import data from other applications into Plant Simulation.
In some cases you will import data into an Plant Simulation list or a table, process it there and then pass it
on to the material flow objects. In other cases you will directly provide imported data to the material flow
objects, for example by using the FileInterface.
You can:
• Import a Text File or an Object File into a List
• Import Data from a Microsoft Excel Worksheet
• Import a List of Services, Shifts, etc. into an Object
• Import Data in XML Format
• Import Data from a Database
• Import or Export Data in ANSI Format
• Import or Export the Contents of a List
Compare Database Interfaces
